f 17592186389760 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198465 1038 #edb/ref 17592186389767 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198567 1068 #edb/ref 17592186194003 13194139533463 17592186045585 false] [17592186198567 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388524 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198567 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198567 1071 "The minimum value of the quadratic form $Q(x) = 3x_{1}^{2} - 2x_{1}x_{2} + 3x_{2}^{2}$, when $‖x‖ = 1$, is equal to $2$. Which of the following is a vector $x$ at which the minimum is attained?" 13194139533463 17592186045585 false] [17592186198567 1071 "The minimum value of the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2},$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to $2.$ Which of the following is a vector $x$ at which the minimum is attained?" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198567 1074 "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n \nThe maximum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-2I & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-2I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$  \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{min}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198696 1068 #edb/ref 17592186194772 13194139533463 17592186045585 false] [17592186198696 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389656 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198696 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198696 1071 "$x$ is positive **and** prime.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $X(x):$ $x$ is positive\n\n- $Y(x):$ $x$ is prime" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198696 1071 "> $x$ is positive **and** prime.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $X(x)$: $x$ is positive\n- $Y(x)$: $x$ is prime" 13194139533463 17592186045585 false] [17592186198696 1074 "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧.$\"\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{X}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{x\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{Y},\n$$\n\nthat is, $X∧Y.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198778 1068 #edb/ref 17592186195318 13194139533463 17592186045585 false] [17592186198778 1068 #edb/ref 17592186195323 13194139533463 17592186045585 false] [17592186198778 1068 #edb/ref 17592186195328 13194139533463 17592186045585 false] [17592186198778 1068 #edb/ref 17592186195333 13194139533463 17592186045585 false] [17592186198778 1068 #edb/ref 17592186195338 13194139533463 17592186045585 false] [17592186198778 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389868 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198778 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389873 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198778 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389878 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198778 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389883 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186198778 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389888 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [175