1072 #uuid "79f4de40-5ae7-517c-ba73-7ba072ef9085" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388645 1074 "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{3}$ can be represented as a $3\\times 3$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i,j,$ and $k$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388646 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388647 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388646 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388648 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388646 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388649 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388646 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388650 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388646 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388651 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388646 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388646 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388646 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388649 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388646 1080 #uuid "526a3986-d118-54c2-816c-e8af8e1acf90" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388647 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388647 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388647 1084 #uuid "29f569dc-d96b-5699-8f3e-20988453e6f3" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388648 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388648 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388648 1084 #uuid "f4534784-1ef8-5838-9e19-8c2c63c1f672" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388649 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388649 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388649 1084 #uuid "e55fa24b-71ff-589e-bcdc-33edef4562e3" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388650 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388650 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388650 1084 #uuid "fc1b70cc-c7b2-5126-9c8d-ae743d8a5383" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388651 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388651 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388651 1084 #uuid "e657140b-6907-548a-af86-930b5db105b8" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388652 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388653 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388652 1069 "q-140073" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388652 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388652 1071 "The standard matrix $T$ of a linear transformation $T$ and the vector $b\\in {R}^{3}$ are given below. Determine if there exists a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ such that $T(x)=b.$\nIn the affirmative case, find the value of $2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ are the components of $x.$  \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388652 1072 #uuid "4027f898-11dc-5b09-bb9b-58bf2f6ee48d" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388652 1074 "Since $T$ is the standard matix of $T,$ we have $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Col}(T).$ In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Im}(T),$ we need to check if the equation $Tx=b$ is consistent. \n\nSo, we find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[T\\,|\\,b],$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 9 & 17\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 9 & 17\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd). Hence, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. \nNow, from the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1-2{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(1-2{x}_{3})+3{x}_{3}=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2+{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the general solution is given by \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2+{x}_{3} \\\\ 1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $T(x)=b.$\n\nFinally, $2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2\\cdot 2+1=5.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388654 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388655 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388656 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388657 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388658 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388653 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388653 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388653 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388658 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388653 1080 #uuid "910d4aaa-e4db-5868-9808-87887da