n{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have been given the following diagonalization of $B:$\n\n$$\nB={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[60]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[40]{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSince $B=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${B}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{B}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{120} & =P{D}^{120}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[60]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[40]{2}\\end{aligned}]}^{120}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}(\\sqrt[60]{2})^{120} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (\\sqrt[40]{2})^{120}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -24 \\\\ 12 & 32\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}40 & 24 \\\\ -48 & -28\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388661 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388662 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388663 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388664 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388665 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388660 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17