}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388708 1072 #uuid "3fe32d4d-9284-57a0-89e5-58bdfd98337d" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388708 1074 "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}20 & -36 \\\\ 14 & -25\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388709 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388710 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388709 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388711 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388709 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388712 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388709 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388713 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388709 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388714 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388709 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388709 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388709 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388710 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388709 1080 #uuid "6811151d-cd95-5e12-aa34-9045fdbee48f" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388710 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}20 & -36 \\\\ 14 & -25\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388710 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388710 1084 #uuid "39af9a4f-5bb0-5f67-b99e-b356fdeef13f" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388711 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}20 & 36 \\\\ -25 & 14\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388711 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388711 1084 #uuid "24019f33-d58e-5c2e-9bc0-2466a9447e60" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388712 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}14 & -25 \\\\ 20 & -36\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388712 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388712 1084 #uuid "9eb9cc07-a4ed-5da6-b193-1c9894ee42b4" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388713 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}14 & -36 \\\\ 20 & -25\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388713 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388713 1084 #uuid "1667976f-4e72-5f00-aab0-1b8c12345f8d" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388714 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}25 & -36 \\\\ 14 & -20\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388714 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388714 1084 #uuid "d77416b1-f86b-5a81-a593-653abb91c3eb" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388715 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388716 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388715 1069 "q-140466" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388715 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388715 1071 "Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]$ is a non-zero  vector that is orthogonal to the set $W={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]},$ find the value of $\\frac{b+c}{a}.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388715 1072 #uuid "de22f8a7-0462-58b6-8ab0-2cf50f198a6b" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388715 1074 "The vector $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W$ if $u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0$ and $u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ⇔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & \\frac{7}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & \\frac{7}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{5}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{6}{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{x}_{3} \