aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\ne C,\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda })\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=C.\n$$\n\nSo, our rotation-scaling matrix $C$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\overset{―}{\\lambda }=2-3\\text{i},$ \n the complex conjugate of $\\lambda .$ Hence, to construct the matrix $P,$ we use the eigenvector $\\overset{―}{v},$ the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nNext, we find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{v} & =[\\begin{aligned}-1-2\\text{i} \\\\ 2-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v})}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v}) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v}) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388751 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388752 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388751 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388753 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388751 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388754 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388751 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388755 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388751 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388756 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388751 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388751 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388751 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388755 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388751 1080 #uuid "66b0905b-9058-5e15-92b6-332aab984e53" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388752 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\