3463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388763 1074 "The principal axes of a curve define a coordinate system in which the curve can be represented by its (simplest) canonical equation. \n\nOur curve is an ellipse. This curve will have the canonical equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nif the axes pass through the opposite vertices of the ellipse.\n\n![](images/68/686c221d813d00c6bda5d9f1762fd8b327f85c8bc86a6e05aed5239028a896ba.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388765 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388766 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388767 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388768 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388769 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388764 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388764 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388764 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388769 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388764 1080 #uuid "2960fe39-4842-53e6-a9f3-c1df3c8a0aaa" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388765 1081 "images/79/79858f004c47944a53fa4cb5f85efcf8ea562c2f1cdf519d06495bfa93c8c005.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388765 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388765 1084 #uuid "66278037-da29-5141-928b-17cedf1b9cf2" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388766 1081 "images/22/226990bb31d35aa5374377b3df6eb5cc41a93ee28c363f0be81e275b8ffc8d89.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388766 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388766 1084 #uuid "73b2843f-e787-5fd9-b225-9e330c587a15" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388767 1081 "images/85/85c2faf0ffd691c2ac3b9934a21c965e7298dd06b1644a7f5d1f6e417696ee93.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388767 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388767 1084 #uuid "7798430c-db7c-54b4-aac4-2cd892d04cee" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388768 1081 "images/24/244afb477fee384908651d29418d155bc302bc9e3e6cb1a7cfe6718d9848f473.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388768 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388768 1084 #uuid "1d917d91-606d-5c20-975e-911252dada6a" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388769 1081 "images/68/686c221d813d00c6bda5d9f1762fd8b327f85c8bc86a6e05aed5239028a896ba.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388769 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388769 1084 #uuid "c059bcde-8723-51d0-a72e-035bb81bc1e2" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388770 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388771 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388770 1069 "q-140570" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388770 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388770 1071 "![](images/8b/8b7b81c97a842b82c2e4cbbd041883c1bd7f4f4ab58dc6592c12ec1cc0262620.png)\n\nWhich integral expression gives the total area enclosed between the curve $y={x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x$ and the $x$-axis, as shown above?" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388770 1072 #uuid "258bdd1d-0804-5b67-a22c-b1970d1d2fe6" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388770 1074 "First, we find the limits of integration. We find the $x$-intercepts of the curve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-2x-3) & =0 \\\\ x(x+1)(x-3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $x=-1,x=0$ or $x=3.$ Since $0\\in [-1,3],$ we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=0.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=3.$\n\nFor $x\\in [-1,0]$, we have\n\n$$\n{A}_{1}={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNotice that for $x\\in [0,3]$ the region lies completely below the $x$-axis. Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative. Therefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\n{A}_{2}=-{\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{3}-({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, the total area is\n\n$$\nA={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}-({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388771 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388772 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388771 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388773 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388771 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388774 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388771 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388775 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388771 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388776 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388771 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388771 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388771 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388772 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388771 1080 #uuid "526936f7-c53e-5694-96ec-8ef1e6fae548" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388772 1081 "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}-({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388772 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388772 1084 #uuid "61031960-3fc5-5fe0-95f0-0c7a9b0ff0c7" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388773 1081 "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}-({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388773 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388773 1084 #uuid "4f1349b9-6291-569c-83ec-402833cb45ee" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388774 1081 "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}-({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388774 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388774 1084 #uuid "3a27a3d1-fcad-5965-8194-a093aa94c3c6" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388775 1081 "{\\int }_{-1}^{3}({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388775 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388775 1084 #uuid "8d6b0ffa-adf7-5365-8a98-eaad1b7e3753" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388776 1081 "{\\int }_{-3}^{1}-({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388776 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388776 1084 #uuid "28d80879-289e-5661-89df-3713590efed8" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388777 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388778 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388777 1069 "q-140583" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388777 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388777 1071 "![](images/8b/8b729d243b344df6b26757773bf0521dea80da34fc727541d24babd3732563cf.png)\n\nThe total area $A$ of the region between the curve $y=4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}$ and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=\\frac{5}{2}$ is given by the integral expression below. What is the value of $a?$\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-1}^{a}(4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4})\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{a}^{5/2}(4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4})\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388777 1072 #uuid "cb68cdd3-2757-5be6-bde1-043b15f42f06" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388777 1074 "To determine the missing limit of integration, we need to find the $x$-intercept of the curve $y=4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4} & =-4 \\\\ {x}^{4} & =16 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{{x}^{4}} & =\\pm \\sqrt[4]{16} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt[4]{{2}^{4}} \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution between $x=-1$ and $x=\\frac{5}{2}$ is $x=2.$\n\nSince $2\\in [-1,\\frac{5}{2}],$ we have two regions:\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=2.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=2$ to $x=\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nSo, $a=2$ and the final expression will be\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-1}^{2}(4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4})\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{5/2}(4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4})\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388779 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388780 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388781 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388782 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388783 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388778 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388778 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388778 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388780 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388778 1080 #uuid "15b97b39-9214-5cd5-be06-dad9c9ec0e0b" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388779 1081 "\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388779 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388779 1084 #uuid "ed59c0fa-145a-58c6-9183-7a618b9935a9" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388780 1081 "2" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388780 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388780 1084 #uuid "3b2b15db-3e26-5206-ac2f-5ed2fb6e032f" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388781 1081 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388781 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388781 1084 #uuid "ec6c7690-6ae3-52da-bc3d-2f05754b1818" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388782 1081 "\\frac{7}{3}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388782 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388782 1084 #uuid "66ed0fb5-f500-5d8a-908f-f603def527e5" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388783 1081 "\\frac{9}{4}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388783 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388783 1084 #uuid "ef7a63c1-cb03-5469-bed3-2e5a4974c10b" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388784 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388785 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388784 1069 "q-140643" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388784 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388784 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -8 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}11 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A,$ $Σ,$ and $V$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ what is the first column of $U?$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388784 1072 #uuid "869bbc7e-c91d-54b2-899a-a9769b330e78" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388784 1074 "Recall that if $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ and ${\\sigma }_{i}\\ne 0,$ then the $i$th column of $U$ can be found as\n\n$$\n{u}_{i}=\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{i}}A{v}_{i},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${v}_{i}$ is the $i$th column of the matrix $V.$\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=11$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=9.$ Therefore, the first column of $U$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -8 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{22}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388785 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388786 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388785 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388787 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388785 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388788 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388785 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388789 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388785 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388790 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388785 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388785 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388785 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388788 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388785 1080 #uuid "e7af0c55-c0c0-57b2-8764-cee03bfd3605" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388786 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388786 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388786 1084 #uuid "e6055e84-6449-5143-a2b3-46eff0358050" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388787 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388787 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388787 1084 #uuid "1f939b74-aaf7-502f-8564-0b661fd0e6a9" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388788 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388788 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388788 1084 #uuid "02624a8f-1b6a-5107-a65b-691283905860" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388789 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388789 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388789 1084 #uuid "a8527eb6-3fa6-5558-a401-122a4ccf2932" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388790 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388790 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388790 1084 #uuid "2499ff1e-f85f-5965-ad45-394bcfc443a3" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388791 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388792 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388791 1069 "q-140836" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388791 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388791 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. \nGiven that $D={P}^{T}\\,AP,$ where $P$ is an orthogonal matrix, which of the following could be the third column of the matrix $P?$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388791 1072 #uuid "9299a3a5-08db-5667-adf8-04da51bcb5fa" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388791 1074 "Recall that a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if there exists an orthogonal matrix $P$ such that\n\n$$\nA=PD{P}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a diagonal matrix. Equivalently,\n\n$$\nD={P}^{T}AP.\n$$\n\nMoreover, a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if and only if it is symmetric.\n\nFirst, note that $A$ is symmetric and $D$ is diagonal. Therefore, $D={P}^{T}\\,AP$ gives an orthogonal diagonalization of $A.$\n\nFrom the diagonal matrix $D$ we deduce that the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=0,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=4.$ So, the third column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{3}=4.$ \n\nNow, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{3}=4.$ Computing $A-4I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-4I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-4I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖{v}_{3}‖=\\sqrt{2}.$ Dividing ${v}_{3}$ by its norm, we obtain the third column of $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388792 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388793 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388792 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388794 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388792 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388795 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388792 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388796 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388792 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388797 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388792 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388792 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388792 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388794 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388792 1080 #uuid "d8fd4c90-98c8-5495-9558-4a6d0a8f3d69" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388793 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388793 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388793 1084 #uuid "96e10680-715f-54cb-b957-9869e3d47c73" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true