$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrix $V?$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388819 1072 #uuid "1e53efba-80e2-5d49-ba97-ee657aeabdf1" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388819 1074 "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\\times 3$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 & 10 \\\\ 10 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=2\\sqrt{6}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=2.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=24,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-24I & =[\\begin{aligned}14 & -10 \\\\ 10 & 14\\end{aligned}]-24[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 10 \\\\ 10 & -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-24I)v=0$ gives the unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-4I & =[\\begin{aligned}14 & 10 \\\\ 10 & 14\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 10 \\\\ 10 & 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-4I)v=0$ gives the unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrix $V:$\n\n$$\nV=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388820 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388821 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388820 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388822 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388820 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388823 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388820 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388824 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388820 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388825 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388820 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388820 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388820 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388825 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388820 1080 #uuid "6c5c3228-7a26-54e7-a187-7cc419cf43c6" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388821 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388821 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388821 1084 #uuid "166eb57b-154c-5dff-9b80-1f8ca0845010" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388822 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388822 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388822 1084 #uuid "3387a72d-c34d-5440-b9c6-c13590f43357