of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $4x-2y<6?$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388854 1072 #uuid "1cee14fe-e375-5314-aab5-fe2b10bd1948" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388854 1074 "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2y & <6 \\\\ -2y & <-4x+6 \\\\ 2y & >4x-6 \\\\ y & >2x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line \n\n$$\ny=2x-3.\n$$\n\n Since the inequality involves a 'strictly greater than' sign, the line $y=2x-3$ itself is *not* part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a **dashed line**.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality \n\n$$\ny>2x-3\n$$\n\n refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $y=2x-3,$ so we shade *above* the line.\n\n![](images/2f/2fe69dace2487c1b6dc73fcd122fd358513d8ac9528b3195d2075f8b62c75b4a.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388855 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388856 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388855 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388857 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388855 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388858 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388855 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388859 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388855 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388860 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388855 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388855 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388855 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388859 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388855 1080 #uuid "a9a641e6-d96d-56ee-a09e-0f810a98dfec" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388856 1081 "images/14/1497c291a9a068a414503d3081f52c5df56019d496a3f6c16cc905e6a20b97fe.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388856 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388856 1084 #uuid "18e4d2