ation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ is orthogonal, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -24 \\\\ 24 & -7\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-11 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-(2) & =-11 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388961 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388962 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388963 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388964 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388965 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388960 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388960 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388960 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388963 13194139533463 17592