7592186045585 true] [17592186388978 1084 #uuid "55a3f1da-3779-59ce-ae0d-0dbecdb726b9" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388979 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388979 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388979 1084 #uuid "053ae894-bb63-5ac6-b828-d9ea6bb6af7f" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388980 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388981 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388980 1069 "q-158129" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388980 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388980 1071 "Verify whether the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent, and find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388980 1072 #uuid "7f3f0d39-46aa-5c30-a041-815de875f218" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388980 1074 "First, we verify whether ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, the pivot columns correspond to the linearly independent vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ that form the basis of our span.\n\nNow, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the linearly independent columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388982 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388983 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388984 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388985 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388986 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388981 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388981 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388981 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388983 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388981 1080 #uuid "c310404e-e4a9-55ab-a9ab-4c596d9b583c" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388982 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388982 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388982 1084 #uuid "26b1ea4a-8431-5e9b-892f-bca7c95f80b0" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388983 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388983 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388983 1084 #uuid "a5c9edc5-9c1a-5e2a-b1fe-0d7188e07e9a" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388984 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388984 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388984 1084 #uuid "a1d236a8-2a2f-599a-b81e-073c9d88e925" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388985 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388985 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388985 1084 #uuid "e60312e7-b230-5a43-aa7d-233414826603" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388986 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388986 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388986 1084 #uuid "82820516-f5de-5854-9a60-bb231ec12fc9" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388987 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388988 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388987 1069 "q-158200" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388987 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388987 1071 "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $g(x,y)=\\frac{y}{2-x}?$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388987 1072 #uuid "ddc33dd3-a1a1-567c-a9d1-d5d15d54e87f" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388987 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n2-x\\ne 0\\,⟹\\,x\\ne 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ne 2}.\n$$\n\nSince the expression involves the $\\ne $ sign, the line is *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we draw the dashed line $x=2$ and shade *right* and *left* the line.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/23/2371c9724d66e0f7d74c45e173f9625a986615185c10d55c029976baa82d0877.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388989 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388990 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388991 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388992 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388993 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388988 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388988 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388988 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388990 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388988 1080 #uuid "c35e8875-bbf9-5e5f-bc9a-34467a284be5" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388989 1081 "images/9f/9f4dd7da9adf7ec5580f4e866fdf094e90e87425ce435feae6dc41488e6518bf.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388989 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388989 1084 #uuid "c5fbd44c-edf5-56b4-9863-36a35f3b9ad3" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388990 1081 "images/3e/3e55fa4f75253935fb3f372dd82612b241d1133aceaa51666fdb0513decba8ea.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388990 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388990 1084 #uuid "dce09265-cac3-50b1-9938-d4e109c7378c" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388991 1081 "images/64/6431427a27685248942ae4ac998feeb8f38d210b63e7f4c429ce3a5bf9afd1e5.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388991 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388991 1084 #uuid "6e38f214-36b2-5226-88a7-d7314eed1c5a" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388992 1081 "images/04/04b8028809192321180e05f2e86c5e149b4870ddb0adea7e3191e2db33f12133.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388992 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388992 1084 #uuid "aea45356-e834-5306-9e4b-0c712e35b96f" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388993 1081 "images/91/91094f3f8fc9b21724e4e6d0f33e2ec0dc18782b3cc0aa1d4b1e4226e4bb93bc.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388993 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388993 1084 #uuid "283aafa9-a98b-5196-ab68-7113c77960e4" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388994 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388995 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388994 1069 "q-158202" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388994 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388994 1071 "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-2x)?$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388994 1072 #uuid "fa9a90c8-68ec-5392-a3c8-0ae9ab63850c" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388994 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\ny-2x>0\\,⟹\\,y>2x\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>2x}.\n$$\n\nSince the expression involves