7592186388999 1081 "images/f8/f843c386c730f85e7c3511e4fd8631b01f77b998f4e99fe19ed9783e4c4b6cbb.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388999 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186388999 1084 #uuid "5accd97b-35b2-571d-8505-8db9329051a6" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389000 1081 "images/44/44e6511542b39bb3946095ff28c7a82ab3e35b5e50d648aba246413e6fea00c4.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389000 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389000 1084 #uuid "5eeca2ff-1397-558c-b26b-156e2af27244" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389001 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389002 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389001 1069 "q-158205" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389001 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389001 1071 "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}?$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389001 1072 #uuid "9419d3b0-0595-5357-8a67-2ff487c67499" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389001 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0\\,⟹\\,(x,y)\\ne (0,0)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,(x.y)\\ne (0,0)}.\n$$\n\nSince the expression involves the $\\ne $ sign, the point $(0,0)$ is *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we exclude the point $(x,y)=(0,0)$ and shade the plane.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/70/701c54bff1c431883f21cb980ac43f4f2f6beabb11817066a4e909d5a2663a25.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389002 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389003 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389002 1075 #edb/ref 175921863890