y=u.\n$$\n\nFind the image of $Δ$ under the action of $T.$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$*" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389069 1072 #uuid "5e3c0bea-5d6e-5a25-bcb3-abdcd207f44f" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389069 1074 "We're told that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$ So, to map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we transform each side of $Δ$ separately:\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{1},$ where we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le 1.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,u) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+{0}^{2},\\,u) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,u), & 0\\le u\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a right-opening parabola traversed from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{2}.$ Here, we have $u=1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ Substituting $u=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,u) &  \\\\  & =({1}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,1) &  \\\\  & =(1+{v}^{2},\\,1), & 0\\le v\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a horizontal line segment traversed from the point $(1,1)$ to the point $(2,1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{3}.$ Here, we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,u) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+{1}^{2},\\,u) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+1,\\,u), & 1\\ge u\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a right-opening parabola traversed from the point $(2,1)$ to the point $(1,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{4}.$ Here, we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,u) &  \\\\  & =({0}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,0) &  \\\\  & =({v}^{2},\\,0), & 1\\ge v\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThis is a horizontal line segment traversed from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nDrawing the images of the sides of our square, we obtain the following image of $Δ:$\n\n![](images/56/56f11a4e05de6f090f94d38550b4cd21f042c1acc5d9ae67242de5fe3e9c2e50.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389070 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389071 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389070 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389072 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389070 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389073 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389070 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389074 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389070 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389075 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389070 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389070 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389070 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389074 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389070 1080 #uuid "ef4309d7-1981-54e2-82f3-7e4f837d1ae4" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389071 1081 "images/19/19650cf966c3c455fa859877b4718c08aea8a343876e5817c625618098a84730.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389071 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389071 1084 #uuid "aaf80778-6e4d-52c2-a5db-4a2ef680da77" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389072 1081 "images/9d/9dc7559632cbecf450389f362ca478d40576ac9646489fda281519c48f49eb16.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389072 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389072 1084 #uuid "c91635d8-70ba-5406-b235-c716cd8cb5db" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389073 1081 "images/56/565227489ba6ae7a657a4b2f1e0133bc117e0e666557f58f59ec0272ad8c574e.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389073 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389073 1084 #uuid "a5d4992f-3bd8-5933-9744-bd2784689f3a" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389074 1081 "images/56/56f11a4e05de6f090f94d38550b4cd21f042c1acc5d9ae67242de5fe3e9c2e50.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389074 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389074 1084 #uuid "d9925307-ecfb-5b78-8679-f58cb68b9e83" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389075 1081 "images/eb/eb6908aea50ad1c314efefdaaf922a8c637673a38f76ee8aadcbdc361f44ff78.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389075 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389075 1084 #uuid "f94a3624-0a44-5d1c-a294-b6849858edb7" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389076 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389077 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389076 1069 "q-160634" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389076 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389076 1071 "![](images/5f/5f91cc8b30f9b764021cd84c374a328c7ffb1287a9f0dc6a211a3fadfac2fdbd.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=v(u+1),\\,y={v}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind the image of $Δ$ under the action of $T.$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$*" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389076 1072 #uuid "17778faf-867d-5bf4-a58a-bee309a2767d" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389076 1074 "We're told that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$ So, to map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we transform each side of $Δ$ separately:\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{1},$ where we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le 1.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(v(u+1),\\,{v}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(0(u+1),\\,{0}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(0,\\,0), & 0\\le u\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{2}.$ Here, we have $u=1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ Substituting $u=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(v(u+1),\\,{v}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(v(1+1),\\,{v}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(2v,\\,{v}^{2}), & 0\\le v\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is an upward-opening parabola traversed from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(2,1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{3}.$ Here, we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(v(u+1),\\,{v}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(1(u+1),\\,{1}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(u+1,\\,1), & 1\\ge u\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a horizontal line segment traversed from the point $(2,1)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{4}.$ Here, we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(v(u+1),\\,{v}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(v(0+1),\\,{v}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(v,\\,{v}^{2}), & 1\\ge v\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThis is an upward-opening parabola traversed from the point $(1,1)$ to the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nDrawing the images of the sides of our square, we obtain the following image of $Δ:$\n\n![](images/4a/4a2614c282a7cd82ff52ecacd7135f9c95bce5df5cfa9a06f2824b63c60c6eb2.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389078 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389079 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389080 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389081 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389077 107