-27a3d99136c7" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389249 1074 "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$ This gives\n\n| **$\\theta $** | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ | $\\pi $ | $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$ This gives\n\n| **$\\theta $** | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ | $\\pi $ | $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](images/47/47615688bf550384de29a5e7e480bdab699b8eee994e5e28052e4d043e2db503.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389250 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389251 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389250 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389252 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389250 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389253 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389250 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389254 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389250 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389255 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389250 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389250 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389250 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389253 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389250 1080 #uuid "0654bdfd-e646-5833-bff5-a82fbd058d96" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389251 1081 "images/ec/ecf914db233f7b1775f49b060470af6a244f8ea8d101fdcced746144b0284552.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389251 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389251 1084 #uuid "55564f42-9122-50c8-bc85-7b867e39832a" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389252 1081 "images/f3/f3cd046f58b44ee916b85df91382a16360895b12c8d47a4a25deffe09f7d7c05.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389252 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389252 1084 #uuid "7ce864de-6e2a-5ab7-bcef-4e9face373f7" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389253 1081 "images/e3/e3f30779c39c3800ed3a8f090df581bc9d1b7007e299fd4504180e7be1ec52e9.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389253 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389253 1084 #uuid "97f59338-f537-5bbb-8998-6e13760f227e" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389254 1081 "images/9e/9e5fb2564eb1f5adb380d70e1a86925fa377f10cc653d98d73ba64bfb03de197.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389254 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389254 1084 #uuid "3e2793cd-65cc-58f3-b7c3-b03cb6422420" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389255 1081 "images/27/2733af9666ca54ca578eea56a5f05d5d8245df01f7aa1312e70610ae8a7beee7.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389255 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389255 1084 #uuid "8c4672ba-d70d-5d79-ba28-25b3937fb8e4" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389256 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389257 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389256 1069 "q-162197" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389256 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389256 1071 "![](images/c3/c36f3eb07b45eebf7f4de2a26cb366ca4ab785b5c7e8e6d25eb7bbad2c418838.png)\n\nConsider the affine transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nx=3u-v-1,\\,y=2u+5v.\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the rectangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389256 1072 #uuid "11c11bf3-c97a-56d9-961f-42e1efebf284" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389256 1074 "Recall that for any affine transformation \n\n$$\nT:u⟶Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $u$ and $b$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors, we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., when $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., when $det(A)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $A$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $A$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a point on the plane.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nThe given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v-1 \\\\ 2u+5v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v \\\\ 2u+5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 5-2\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =17 \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a non-singular matrix. \n\nTherefore, $T$ is invertible, and the image of the rectangle under the action of $T$ is a parallelogram." 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389257 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389258 13194139533463 1759218604558