533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389318 1072 #uuid "51e3e7e7-44a6-54ed-a3c2-de6f58c215e2" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389318 1074 "We wish to find limits of integration ${u}_{1}(x,z),$ ${u}_{2}(x,z),$ ${v}_{1}(z),$ ${v}_{2}(z),$ $a,$ and $b$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(z)}^{{v}_{2}(z)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the region of integration $R$ can be written as a type II region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z$ to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z,$ we write $R$ as a type III region and its projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane as a type II *plane* region.\n\nTo visualize this, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $y$-axis and in the direction of increasing $y,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c3837a3551b35a5146fd2c8e2441e4a9d6d947e8c52e44254d48eb854e54e605.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the left boundary and leaves through the right boundary:\n\n- The left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x,z),$ is\n\n$$\nx={y}^{2}\\,⟹\\,y=\\sqrt{x}.\n$$\n\n- The right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,\\sqrt{x}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{2}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/22/22581a56f4d9cb611bd9a58b06b1036cd47b500217570ae6890d0f38dba6742c.png)\n\nWe now consider the projection $D$ as a type II plane region in the $xz$-plane with the right curve given by \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=\\sqrt{x} \\\\ y=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\sqrt{x}=\\sqrt{2}\\,⟹\\,x=2.\n$$\n\n![](images/e2/e2305d3da63886703666fd58a2adfe8f15f2eceb7261922f46ba4949b0fc0cde.png)\n\nHence, we have that\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration so that it is integrated first with respect to $y,$ then $x,$ then $z,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389319 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389320 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389319 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389321 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389319 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389322 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389319 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389323 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389319 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389324 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389319 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389319 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389319 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389321 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389319 1080 #uuid "3e206289-9f04-516a-8774-93cf7cecd07e" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389320 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}{\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389320 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389320 1084 #uuid "9c5e2e70-5ffa-5c48-a5cf-9bd5f4ffb5b4" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389321 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389321 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389321 1084 #uuid "e136e6ca-8d75-50a6-9664-a3d5830c5e29" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389322 1081