 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389339 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389339 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389339 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389341 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389339 1080 #uuid "2e8d4565-bdfe-5e4a-bfbd-afe9b3d061b3" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389340 1081 "t\\in (1,\\infty )" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389340 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389340 1084 #uuid "ed24ecfc-29fd-5287-8375-b97afb7a1ad9" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389341 1081 "t\\in (-1,\\infty )" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389341 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389341 1084 #uuid "7e9431db-9aa7-5e0a-8e08-1ab991e0068f" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389342 1081 "t\\in (-\\infty ,1)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389342 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389342 1084 #uuid "c9c05318-56c4-5ed1-bd19-90eb05aa5fd9" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389343 1081 "t\\in (-\\infty ,-1)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389343 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389343 1084 #uuid "593851d7-7a77-51d3-a640-4a7a63ee05cb" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389344 1081 "t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389344 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389344 1084 #uuid "7bab972e-0930-5dc4-b4ee-926d2ac18fbc" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389345 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389346 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389345 1069 "q-162629" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389345 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389345 1071 "Which of the following represents the streamlines of the vector field $F(x,y)=2xi-2y\\,j$ over the domain $D={R}^{2}.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389345 1072 #uuid "6b93df85-0b3c-5ded-8201-a97d95285f56" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389345 1074 "The streamlines of a vector field are the level curves of its stream function and are tangential to the vector field at every point. \n\nIf $F$ represents the velocity field of a fluid flow, then they show the path traced out by a massless particle as it moves with the flow.\n\nA vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=2xi-2y\\,j\n$$\n\n is a vector field with simply connected domain $D,$ where $P(x,y)=2x$ and $Q(x,y)=-2y.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=2-2=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}=2y.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)=2xy+f(x),\\,ψ(x,y)=2xy+g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f=g=0,$ we have\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)=2xy.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the level curves of the stream function $ψ(x,y)=2xy$ given by the equations $ψ(x,y)=c.$\n\nNotice that the range of $ψ(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(x,y) & =c \\\\ 2xy & =c \\\\ y & =\\frac{c}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of hyperbolas with asymptotes $y=0$ and $x=0$ and, for $c=0,$ the lines $y=0$ and $x=0.$ Therefore, the correct graph (along with the vector field $F$) is as follows:\n\n![](images/24/24c6dadd4f980121a36929a9cdb800f7da8fac8eb84af40d595af89aa77b11ea.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389346 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389347 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389346 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389348 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389346 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389349 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389346 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389350 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389346 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389351 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389346 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389346 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389346 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389350 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389346 1080 #uuid "ce55e1ed-b422-5201-909f-65fba9887b50" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389347 1081 "images/6a/6a1ce9b96f0bca4ec14e7ce60e5cebd72efc4421acfd4a65ba55e9c8a7d1d352.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389347 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389347 1084 #uuid "bc9bdb8d-ad2b-5d91-86ca-825ec11037fa" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389348 1081 "images/07/0799c425e6b33f2be8f115d7d0de9e5607bdef9f094a02381fc5197839d80d75.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389348 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389348 1084 #uuid "678a4e30-3832-553e-8ea1-b4ab930f1cd6" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389349 1081 "images/95/95fee99b51dc07130717569fcb90ab5e210bf2cc64811f536dc493e9c3e1588e.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389349 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389349 1084 #uuid "6db4de8e-dbc7-51ee-8ae9-5b089f44fbf6" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389350 1081 "images/3a/3a3ef451c7e25ff33fb1820d5b8c98e10038c4ee058f627d93acf72989b7b794.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389350 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389350 1084 #uuid "92bd4bba-9b1d-550f-a3d8-850c5ca8fd4d" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389351 1081 "images/fb/fb7119466ac4f884fca55cfb3fc0b487703249050211ff922549a702a047bb39.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389351 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389351 1084 #uuid "1bc3c2dd-f56c-5123-bcfe-941b923629fb" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389352 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389353 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389352 1069 "q-162630" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389352 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389352 1071 "Which of the following represents the streamlines of the vector field $F(x,y)=2y\\,i+2x\\,j$ over the domain $D={R}^{2}.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389352 1072 #uuid "bc28542a-a43a-5f01-b243-0063900eefa8" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389352 1074 "The streamlines of a vector field are the level curves of its stream function and are tangential to the vector field at every point. \n\nIf $F$ represents the velocity field of a fluid flow, then they show the path traced out by a massless particle as it moves with the flow.\n\nA vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=2y\\,i+2x\\,j\n$$\n\n is a vector field with simply connected domain $D,$ where $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=0,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y}=2y,\\,\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}=-2x.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={y}^{2}+f(x),\\,ψ(x,y)=-{x}^{2}+g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f(x)=-{x}^{2}$ or $g(y)={y}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the level curves of the stream function $ψ(x,y)={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}$ given by the equations $ψ(x,y)=c.$\n\nNotice that the range of $ψ(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(x,y) & =c \\\\ {y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of hyperbolas with asymptotes $y=x$ and $x=-x$ and, for $c=0,$ the lines $y=x$ and $y=-x.$ Therefore, the correct graph (along with the vector field $F$) is as follows:\n\n![](images/9b/9b0d2f98a0b71beb773b802908f01691924492a5f3abff3db75be4a0ae458e7d.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389353 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389354 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389353 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389355 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389353 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389356 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389353 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389357 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389353 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389358 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389353 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389353 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389353 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389355 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389353 1080 #uuid "f9db8e2f-b628-5684-b658-6125f7acf877" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389354 1081 "images/32/3296bdd0ae6e92949ee3728e01592f1758917cf03446e75317af341ef669f606.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389354 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389354 1084 #uuid "0b9a4a14-a956-5391-ac3a-4943156bef2b" 13194139533463 175921860