true] [17592186389455 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389455 1071 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis under the action of a force of magnitude $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{N}$ acting in the direction of increasing $x.$ Given that $x$ is measured in meters, calculate the work done by the force in moving the particle from $x=1$ to $x=4.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389455 1072 #uuid "d31a00a5-c404-50d8-b7f2-fda34cf2cc53" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389455 1074 "The work done by a force $F=F(x)$ in moving a particle from $x={x}_{1}$ to $x={x}_{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nW={\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}F(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhen the force and distance are measured in Newtons and meters, respectively, the work done by the force is measured in Joules ($J$).\n\nSubstituting the given values into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{4}-1) \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\,J.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389456 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389457 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389456 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389458 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389456 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389459 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389456 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389460 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389456 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389461 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389456 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389456 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389456 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389457 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389456 1080 #uuid "7fc72668-2f1d-508f-943f-15caead3623c" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389457 1081 "\\frac{3}{4}\\,J" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389457 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389457 1084 #uuid "eb4d826c-14ba-585c-aebd-1facb3368012" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389458 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}\\,J" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389458 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389458 1084 #uuid "8ab762ed-0112-5d52-b62f-05b3b484b0b7" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389459 1081 "2\\,J" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389459 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389459 1084 #uuid "6aa053a0-465d-5f0b-8742-c3a588a86e3e" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389460 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}\\,J" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389460 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389460 1084 #uuid "ee6add72-368a-56d1-a701-8e8fbe0ceee5" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389461 1081 "3\\,J" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389461 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389461 1084 #uuid "04400f5c-b01f-5a74-aa41-074c903d6463" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389462 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389463 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389462 1069 "q-163702" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389462 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389462 1071 "A particle $P$ of mass $1\\,kg$ moves along the $x$-axis under the action of the force of magnitude $(3{x}^{2}+2)\\,N$ acting in the direction of increasing $x.$ Given that distances along the $x$-axis are measured in meters, the particle is initially at the origin, and the particle has velocity $v=7\\,m/s$ at $x=2,$ find the particle's change in velocity in moving from $x=0$ to $x=2.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389462 1072 #uuid "89e50146-b1c6-571f-ad82-cc9a4f7f02cf" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389462 1074 "The work-energy principle states that the work done by a resultant force on a particle equals the change in the particle's kinetic energy. That is,\n\n$$\nW=Δ\\,\\text{KE}\n$$\n\nwhere the change in kinetic energy of a particle is given by\n\n$$\nΔ\\,\\text{KE}=\\frac{1}{2}m{v}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}m{v}_{0}^{2}\n$$\n\nand $m$ is the particle's mass, ${v}_{0}$ is its initial velocity, and ${v}_{1}$ is its final velocity.\n\nFirst, we calculate the work done by the force in moving the particle from $x=0$ to $x=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & ={\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}F(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}+2x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =8+4-0 \\\\  & =12\\,J\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle has velocity $v=7\\,m/s$ at $x=2.$ So, we can find the velocity ${v}_{0}$ at $x=0$ using the work-energy principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =\\frac{1}{2}m{v}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}m{v}_{0}^{2} \\\\ 12 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1\\cdot {7}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1\\cdot {v}_{0}^{2} \\\\ 12 & =\\frac{49}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{0}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{v}_{0}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{2} \\\\ {v}_{0}^{2} & =25 \\\\ {v}_{0} & =\\pm 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can disregard the negative solution since the velocity and acceleration of the particle are positive in the regions under consideration. \n\nTherefore, the velocity of the particle at $x=0$ is $5\\,m/s.$\n\nFinally, the particle's change in velocity from $x=0$ to $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}-{v}_{0}=7-5=2\\,m/s.\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389463 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389464 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389463 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389465 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389463 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389466 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389463 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389467 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389463 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389468 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389463 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389463