[17592186389510 1072 #uuid "c3e82248-046d-51ec-a301-4e2c4f12e087" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389510 1074 "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nSince the mass density is symmetric in $x$ and $y,$ the center of mass is at $(0,0).$ The mass density function, in polar coordinates, is given by \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{|r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta |}{{r}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|.\n$$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{r}^{2}{|}_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2-1)\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(4-1)\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $3\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+{3}^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+9 \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389512 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389513 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389514 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389515 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389516 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389511 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389511 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389511 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389514 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389511 1080 #uuid "6f30222c-68be-5948-ada7-44c499e54de9" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389512 1081 "\\frac{25}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389512 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389512 1084 #uuid "73d53966-105e-5278-a8b5-9492f93a8b