{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nfor $x\\ge 3$ in $xy$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=⟨3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =\\frac{(3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9{sec}^{2}⁡t}{9}-\\frac{2{tan}^{2}⁡t}{2} \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡t-{tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,z) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389519 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389520 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389521 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389522 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389523 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389518 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389518 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389518 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389522 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389518 1080 #uuid "b92fac85-7a9a-5915-90d4-a283e5eef049" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389519 1081 "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389519 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389519 1084 #uuid "9b007fc6-a9cf-594b-9130-ef77ac13f04c" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389520 1081 "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" 13194139533463 1759218