atural number $m,$ we have that ${100}^{m}$ is a perfect square.\n\nNow, \"${100}^{m}$ is a perfect square\" means that\n\nThere exists an integer number $n$ such that ${100}^{m}={n}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we get the following statement:\n\nFor any natural number $m,$ there exists an integer $n$ such that ${100}^{m}={n}^{2}.$\n\nMore formally, this reads as\n\n$∀\\,m\\in N,\\,∃\\,n\\in Z,\\,{100}^{m}={n}^{2}.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389711 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389712 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389713 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389714 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389715 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389710 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389710 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389710 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389715 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389710 1080 #uuid "c499b3d0-3890-5f95-bbdc-a6a512cd5b9c" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389711 1081 "∃\\,m\\in N,\\,∀\\,n\\in Z,\\,{100}^{m}=n" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389711 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389711 1084 #uuid "318e6947-a97e-5c0c-98e5-62329ae4629e" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389712 1081 "∃\\,m\\in N,\\,∀\\,n\\in Z,\\,{100}^{m}={n}^{2}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389712 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389712 1084 #uuid "bbea2909-6211-532c-8ad9-d5109ee79161" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389713 1081 "∀\\,m\\in N,\\,∃\\,n\\in Z,\\,100={n}^{2}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389713 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389713 1084 #uuid "bcf7c031-9068-5c4c-9e0d-78348f6962f2" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389714 1081 "∀\\,m\\in N,\\,∃\\,n\\in Z,\\,{100}^{m}=n" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389714 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389714 1084 #uuid "0404c4c6-6289-5160-a30f-b7eae8a48f15" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389715 1081 "∀\\,m\\in N,\\,∃\\,n\\in Z,\\,{100}^{m}={n}^{2}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389715 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389715 1084 #uuid "6a2dcd54-0589-53d0-b8b2-ceeb42eee87a" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389716 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389717 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389716 1069 "q-175380" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389716 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389716 1071 "$x$ is less than $1,$ **or** $x$ is even **or**  prime.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $L(x):$ $x$ is less than $1$\n\n- $E(x):$ $x$ is even\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is prime" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389716 1072 #uuid "de46e6cd-5305-5c67-9e7b-98d46fc43965" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389716 1074 "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts: \n\n- **Part 1:**  $x$ is less than $1.$ This corresponds to $L.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is even or prime. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\,\\text{is even}}_{⏟}}_{E}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\,\\text{is prime}}_{⏟}}_{P},\n$$\n\nthat is, $E∨P.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is less than }1}_{⏟}}_{L}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\,\\text{is even or prime}}_{⏟}}_{E∨P},\n$$\n\nthat is, $L∨E∨P.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389717 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389718 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389717 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389719 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389717 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389720 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389717 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389721 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389717 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389722 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389717 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389717 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389717 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389720 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389717 1080 #uuid "0814b16b-b84a-50f0-89ee-6bebde44015c" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389718 1081 "L∨(E∧P)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389718 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389718 1084 #uuid "f8a4d09b-80d2-5f19-b45f-05317454b827" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389719 1081 "(L∨E)∧P" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389719 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389719 1084 #uuid "b7971a96-a768-5469-8f3e-a3e783e9b4d7" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389720 1081 "L∨E∨P" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389720 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389720 1084 #uuid "36e425de-0e80-5a0b-86e9-e872104cb553" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389721 1081 "(L∧E)∨P" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389721 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389721 1084 #uuid "a6250575-900c-5544-b04c-18b583f55c2c" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389722 1081 "L∧E∧P" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389722 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389722 1084 #uuid "c70cd278-4590-58e6-9b87-682c16024743" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389723 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389724 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389723 1069 "q-17556" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389723 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389723 1071 "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y}{x}+x{y}^{2},\\,y(1)=2,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that the given differential equation can be transformed into the equation*\n\n$$\n\\frac{dz}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}z=-x\n$$\n\n*using the substitution $z={y}^{-1}.$*" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389723 1072 #uuid "d5c02985-b98e-5a6d-903a-448a7295c82b" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389723 1074 "The substitution $z={y}^{-1}$ transforms the given equation into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dz}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}z=-x.\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=-x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nunder the condition that $x>0.$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{dz}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot (-x) \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{dz}{dx}+z & =-{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{d}{dx}(xz) & =-{x}^{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(xz)\\,dx & =-\\int {x}^{2}dx \\\\ xz & =-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-{x}^{3}}{3x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nNow, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =\\frac{C-{x}^{3}}{3x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{3x}{C-{x}^{3}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now determine $C$ from the initial condition $y(1)=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{3}{C-1}\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{3x}{(\\frac{5}{2}-{x}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6x}{5-2{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389725 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389726 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389727 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389728 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389729 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389724 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389724 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389724 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389726 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389724 1080 #uuid "8b6edc8e-e15a-59f4-94d1-b264af8881fc" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389725 1081 "y=\\frac{x}{5-2{x}^{3}}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389725 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389725 1084 #uuid "0343692c-a358-56cc-ad31-3caa8d37ff99" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389726 1081 "y=\\frac{6x}{5-2{x}^{3}}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389726 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389726 1084 #uuid "afa1e3c3-2e37-5ac7-8e1d-fc0face1926d" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389727 1081 "y=\\frac{2}{x}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389727 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389727 1084 #uuid "f8bf87b0-1d98-5426-8046-486143ddf661" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389728 1081 "y=\\frac{2x}{2-{x}^{3}}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389728 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389728 1084 #uuid "7bc552c2-315e-5895-974e-defd34743230" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389729 1081 "y=\\frac{2x}{3-2{x}^{2}}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389729 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389729 1084 #