81 "images/58/5888cf137eea674995b4c9cc37285b4130df5de3a2a2fa63b1b5b195910526c1.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389928 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389928 1084 #uuid "51564c2b-bcad-5e6e-9c34-dbd7a16d3a00" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389929 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389930 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389929 1069 "q-181985" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389929 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389929 1071 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=[-1,0]\\times [-1,1]$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389929 1072 #uuid "c70aae50-ffb5-59f2-930c-cbbe5d9bb642" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389929 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=[-1,0]\\times [-1,1]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,0]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,0],\\,y\\in [-1,1]}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}={(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/c9/c93f3ad399b88ccbaac990f8f73e93cfdcb1192f52b9b12f2d3ce178776fa13b.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in [-1,0]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}={(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in [-1,0],$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line segment from the point $(i,-1)$ to the point $(i,1).$\n\n![](images/65/6557201d202a401a92ee37c9a69eab9ab6ab87c6342dbb9d2afebae30141346f.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $I=[-1,0]:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following rectangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/97/97a74b119ddb8a618d6564bc077d03a5a4ceb7152702beb3682f2eab1a436b70.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389931 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389932 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389933 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389934 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389935 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389930 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389930 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389930 1079 #edb/ref 17592186389933 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389930 1080 #uuid "46ec56ed-6fc0-52ed-aa83-998bc8081175" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389931 1081 "images/96/96a29779da824d7d2dc7b6d4f2b9c781a4a593b58e44f491724221c77888e3e3.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389931 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389931 1084 #uuid "72d6c485-e050-55c8-9679-fd6d97aa00e0" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389932 1081 "images/e5/e5b130683075dd04e4b5129065d32b4d75b3dabfaff0b05b90de858b5e0f2961.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389932 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389932 1084 #uuid "08a4e04e-4888-5403-95d8-f078acf2c991" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389933 1081 "images/97/97a74b119ddb8a618d6564bc077d03a5a4ceb7152702beb3682f2eab1a436b70.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186389933 1083 #edb/ref 175921