[17592186390529 1084 #uuid "e4093346-6cc0-5f63-9423-7b76da2a672f" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390530 1081 "images/bb/bbdfe3e538e840385c082f16ca2cdfd07a7731c561d05cab6e7a25f487cdf463.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390530 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390530 1084 #uuid "fd28d0fd-5ee9-586e-ade7-f559ef7573ec" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390531 1081 "images/cd/cd11656e3dae8a4976b1051a135b4bead1e5afc4beb21fa7541571892a037500.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390531 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390531 1084 #uuid "be9702e6-d21c-5c09-a96e-1267b5361dc9" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390532 1081 "images/66/6674add26b7a15f5b09c53a832d649979484f0ffd41b440069dd5230cd9a5187.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390532 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390532 1084 #uuid "35b1a419-9084-5fab-a034-b69305bdd882" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390533 1081 "images/a3/a30938f3d3af2fd70a0ee9498d7d99973d5386f062f22aaa8a028e9e18b3fb57.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390533 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390533 1084 #uuid "724df295-2359-5b8b-ab62-27d9d0e10f5e" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390534 1068 #edb/ref 17592186390535 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390534 1069 "q-270439" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390534 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390534 1071 "According to the rational root theorem, the polynomial $f(x)=49{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-5x+7$ has{{field-1}} *potential* rational roots." 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390534 1072 #uuid "612bf785-43c9-5609-bd69-355f15a47984" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390534 1074 "Given a polynomial with integer coefficients, the rational roots theorem states that any rational roots of the polynomial must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial:\n\n- The constant term is $7,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1$ and $\\pm 7.$\n\n- The leading coefficient is $49,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1$, $\\pm 7$ and $\\pm 49.$\n\nFirst, we list out all the possibilities for the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm \\frac{1}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{7}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{49}, \\\\ \\pm \\frac{7}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{7}{7}, & \\pm \\frac{7}{49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we reduce the fractions to their lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{1}{7}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{49}, \\\\ \\pm 7, & \\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{1}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that some potential roots are duplicates (shown above in red). Removing these duplicates and listing those remaining in order from least to greatest in absolute value, we have\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{1}{49},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{7},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm 7.\n$$\n\nThis makes a total of $8$ potential roots. (Remember that each $\\pm $ sign accounts for $2$ roots, and $2\\cdot 4=8.$)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390535 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390536 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390535 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390535 1077 "field-1" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390535 1079 #edb/ref 17592186390536 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390535 1080 #uuid "ace71b7c-8f1f-5f7b-b5d8-3a10944ba75b" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390536 1081 "8" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390536 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390536 1084 #uuid "858c261e-14be-5341-b40a-d550c565ee07" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390537 1068 #edb/ref 17592186390538 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390537 1069 "q-27477" 131941