 to $(0,-\\frac{5}{2})$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-3.$\n\n![](images/e5/e545a84145ac0a139ee5ecdf9692c20837d211f9a70fd79ad33dd13f60c856f7.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390552 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390553 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390552 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390554 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390552 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390555 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390552 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390556 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390552 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390557 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390552 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390552 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390552 1079 #edb/ref 17592186390553 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390552 1080 #uuid "b29207c3-5e76-521f-8c52-fed97e9cf151" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390553 1081 "images/e5/e545a84145ac0a139ee5ecdf9692c20837d211f9a70fd79ad33dd13f60c856f7.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390553 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390553 1084 #uuid "0f70e31a-a6d8-57be-8930-fe9e46798cf1" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390554 1081 "images/f6/f63e49a2e8f4a0702841eb132093bf6f69b8405af25719ea8f5abbf2bd691122.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390554 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390554 1084 #uuid "3dd43261-0c67-5dec-abd5-e030f8c694d1" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390555 1081 "images/c6/c64e79b7c0069aaf7d4393a6879612f58f48103247b1ba7efef3531dc3986b93.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390555 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390555 1084 #uuid "c08648ea-dc6d-5578-89fa-a0be944fb62c" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390556 1081 "images/57/571e2268e6b7f41e80b71c8764d321c298fe58232e5b4c5a84ce309fa0dd3530.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390556 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390556 1084 #uuid "84311dad-8f82-5f9c-ab3a-b304e0b27aae" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390557 1081 "images/3d/3d7af2718ba7c30956218a00da51e77db950183bd2a85dbe74107e493fd5f03b.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390557 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390557 1084 #uuid "8b546f29-cf64-542e-8f37-af2b900bcda8" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390558 1068 #edb/ref 17592186390559 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390558 1069 "q-276773" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390558 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390558 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{x-8}{7-2x}.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$  \n{{field-1}}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390558 1072 #uuid "212d9c4b-4962-5204-87c1-b501c43df724" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390558 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x-8}{7-2x}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{y-8}{7-2y}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{y-8}{7-2y} \\\\ x(7-2y) & =y-8 \\\\ 7x-2xy & =y-8 \\\\ 7x+8 & =y+2xy \\\\ 7x+8 & =y(2x+1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{7x+8}{2x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{7x+8}{2x+1}.\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390559 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390560 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390559 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390559 1077 "field-1" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390559 1079 #edb/ref 17592186390560 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390559 1080 #uuid "5a777dc6-b24f-5e76-b2c6-6cf6f51d1959" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390560 1081 "\\frac{7x+8}{2x+1}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390560 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390560 1084 #uuid "f55e55c0-cf66-509a-9583-baf6c0228213" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390561 1068 #edb/ref 17592186390562 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390561 1069 "q-276812" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390561 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390561 1071 "The multiplicity of the root $x=5$ in the polynomial $p(x)={x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+5x+50$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390561 1072 #uuid "1be43615-7dc6-54e4-af72-5f8d6df002b4" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390561 1074 "Since $x=5$ is a root of $p(x),$ the factor theorem tells us that $(x-5)$ is a factor of $p(x).$\n\nBecause $(x-5)$ is a factor of $p(x),$ we know that $(x-5)$ divides $p(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $p(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-5)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $1$ | $-8$ | $5$ | $-50$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $5$ | $-15$ | $-50$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-3$ | $-10$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{p(x)}{x-5}={x}^{2}-3x-10,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\np(x)=(x-5)({x}^{2}-3x-10).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =(x-5)(x+2)(x-5) \\\\  & =(x+2)(x-5)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $(x-5)$ has an exponent of $2$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=5$ has multiplicity $2.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390562 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390563 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390562 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390562 1077 "field-1" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390562 1079 #edb/ref 17592186390563 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390562 1080 #uuid "e5657504-e53c-5b3b-93ca-e3c99a9797ea" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390563 1081 "2" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390563 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390563 1084 #uuid "47f617f4-9e85-5721-805a-de7db4f879fb" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390564 1068 #edb/ref 17592186390565 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390564 1069 "q-278288" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390564 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390564 1071 "![](images/ba/ba82c6b68026b0f4339c1e4fa01c4b1aa1b7aee74b74176f81bba1c0e1de259f.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=r,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OS}=s$ and $V$ divides $\\overset{―}{RS}$ in the ratio $RV:VS=6:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OV}.$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390564 1072 #uuid "c822bdd5-b239-5109-a43e-980b6e32d798" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390564 1074 "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OV}=\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RV}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=r,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{RV}.$\n\nFirst, from $△ORS,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RS} & =\\overset{\\to }{RO}+\\overset{\\to }{OS} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{OS} \\\\  & =-r+s \\\\  & =s-r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $RV:VS=6:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RV}=\\frac{6}{11}\\overset{\\to }{RS}=\\frac{6}{11}(s-r).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OV} & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RV} \\\\  & =r+\\frac{6}{11}(s-r) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{11}r+\\frac{6}{11}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390565 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390566 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390565 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390567 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390565 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390568 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390565 