] [17592186390618 1068 #edb/ref 17592186390619 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390618 1069 "q-31468" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390618 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390618 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y={3}^{x+5}-4?$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390618 1072 #uuid "3271be04-4d4e-529b-98e8-aeb7a846817c" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390618 1074 "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- First, we plot the graph of $y={3}^{x}.$\n\n![](images/56/56f4446a00c12419f722dfd008e3cde785e759aa037fedd47911f0a783f4dfed.png)\n\n- To plot $y={3}^{x+5},$ we shift the graph of $y={3}^{x}$ horizontally by $5$ units to the left. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(-5,1),$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/87/871fe4053ba868f475ded7f0722ab7df20636a4db743f10c7631dede279715f1.png)\n\n- To plot $y={3}^{x+5}-4,$ we shift the graph of $y={3}^{x+5}$ vertically by $4$ units down. The point $(-5,1)$ moves to $(-5,-3)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-4.$\n\n![](images/32/3278d9e3e73ffee57ece6d0abf3343f8315c729e694f111dacef0e759dbe4ab4.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390619 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390620 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390619 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390621 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390619 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390622 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390619 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390623 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390619 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390624 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390619 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390619 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390619 1079 #edb/ref 17592186390620 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186390619 1080 #uuid "03c22286-7565-5727-9f06-a11ad4db1ba3" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [175921863