139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391044 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391046 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391044 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391047 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391044 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391048 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391044 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391044 1077 "field-2" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391044 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391047 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391044 1080 #uuid "5f45eed4-80c2-5997-82a1-8910e993b93e" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391045 1081 "-4x" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391045 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391045 1084 #uuid "fcd393be-3f3a-5d54-b56c-765a247c93c8" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391046 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}x" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391046 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391046 1084 #uuid "183836bd-4e06-5498-b5e5-9271bdc51698" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391047 1081 "4x" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391047 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391047 1084 #uuid "35fcaa94-30df-5985-a1d8-53fde28177f4" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391048 1081 "-\\frac{1}{4}x" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391048 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391048 1084 #uuid "e357655c-0a16-56e0-819e-312ae458e498" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391049 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391050 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391049 1069 "q-332683" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391049 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391049 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-7y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391049 1072 #uuid "3f7b6c7b-9bbd-58e1-9f4f-ab6d8faeb7f9" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391049 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=-7$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-7t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis. Since ${e}^{2t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-7t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis. Since ${e}^{-7t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/d6/d604781deed3206caf0a3bf6afa857c00beca9d532a26dedef5c717b4f684225.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391050 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391051 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391050 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391052 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391050 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391053 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391050 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391054 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391050 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391055 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391050 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391050 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391050 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391054 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391050 1080 #uuid "23f7e5e5-ba46-5c75-bde7-3c2b00f02f16" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391051 1081 "images/7c/7c483bbf926df156b7f85fbedcbb6ab18571ff4f544416cd8ea554b70b59a589.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391051 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391051 1084 #uuid "50c7bc7d-0232-5fe1-a6d4-6f9a22440550" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391052 1081 "images/27/27c6bf8d11d3de50beac351f88104df58cac31053eb6ecfc3a35ce77ccd8600b.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391052 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391052 1084 #uuid "9c4028ce-9f71-5bd4-ad6b-47272c4ba666" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391053 1081 "images/01/01d93cb2e68123b061b057ce30b94bcce44401b2d0fc0c566b3c33478c07fb92.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391053 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391053 1084 #uuid "f48f6682-16a0-5a4e-b948-d2adbb5ee402" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391054 1081 "images/d6/d604781deed3206caf0a3bf6afa857c00beca9d532a26dedef5c717b4f684225.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391054 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391054 1084 #uuid "4d70c978-6c43-538a-a72f-3e3d73db9a61" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391055 1081 "images/38/389d3cfc92ece3a63300767f92c34c11dccec981ac43f3f66a2ced02906f8a73.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391055 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391055 1084 #uuid "e571bbe0-b813-51a0-a84b-7bcbc9e1fb37" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391056 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391057 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391056 1069 "q-332709" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391056 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391056 1071 "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391056 1072 #uuid "5620c47b-4e97-5ced-9381-5d5cc172acfd" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391056 1074 "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =(-3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391057 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391058 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391057 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391059 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391057 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391060 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391057 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391061 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391057 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391062 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391057 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391057 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391057 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391061 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391057 1080 #uuid "6964b2cb-9fd8-5726-b5f5-384b2f89e701" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391058 1081 "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391058 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391058 1084 #uuid "7e380f8b-d71f-55a2-ab1b-39f34cd89e65" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391059 1081 "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391059 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391059 1084 #uuid "0f9827f0-71cf-5847-85bc-980bee16161f" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391060 1081 "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391060 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391060 1084 #uuid "ca29bc6f-4907-5a9b-91bf-39c3f6d764fa" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391061 1081 "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391061 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391061 1084 #uuid "b312d8e4-025a-5e6d-99d6-bb6fe41ba80f" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391062 1081 "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391062 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391062 1084 #uuid "755f8ee4-1bac-5f8b-adc2-777c045fa529" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391063 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391064 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391063 1069 "q-332751" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391063 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391063 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=7y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391063 1072 #uuid "7a71e1e9-c69e-580f-aa68-2f882f086377" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391063 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=7$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis. Since ${e}^{3t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis. Since ${e}^{7t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, there are two phase portraits satisfying these conditions:\n\n![](images/96/96801605aa5d777eb18c13ded1f7b7e59ae74968b210da3b7a26f339a1c9f673.png)\n\nLet's consider the solutions $x(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{3t}$ and $y(t)={c}_{2}{e}^{7t}$ provided that ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\ne 0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}=\\frac{({c}_{2}{e}^{7t})^{′}}{({c}_{1}{e}^{3t})^{′}}=\\frac{7{c}_{2}{e}^{7t}}{3{c}_{1}{e}^{3t}}=\\frac{7{c}_{2}}{3{c}_{1}}{e}^{4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\to \\pm \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ meaning that the tangents to the solution become more and more vertical as we move away from the origin. This corresponds to the following phase portrait:\n\n![](images/20/20ef7519d0ca517d0d7d06d2998f7bd6c77f04145243f721e197fbef5c087791.png)" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391064 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391065 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391064 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391066 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391064 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391067 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391064 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391068 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391064 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391069 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391064 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391064 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391064 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391069 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391064 1080 #uuid "9b3e8fa4-883f-5cc4-809d-2815c7f4d579" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391065 1081 "images/9f/9fb1f3c545855e7bdfe591574a9069e69bdcc0cc750e5fc4f5aa3eccfdc7ea5a.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391065 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391065 1084 #uuid "007e1a63-77b7-5eff-8905-bffd2a2a8d59" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391066 1081 "images/ec/eceeabfeb428687bb9f630fe3578937c3fd4fb910605dc25daf56ad5ce18a68a.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391066 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391066 1084 #uuid "b3aa6c52-d997-5f86-9c55-1e2a11e1e45b" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391067 1081 "images/64/64c0ac27236c4bfae45257