376a2392bad1b159123da933c6defb7145cc6ab6ce2634.png" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391142 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391142 1084 #uuid "e8cbcbee-4126-5a07-ad49-6ed0503afbbe" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391143 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391144 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391143 1069 "q-333120" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391143 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391143 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{3}+{x}^{2},\\,y(1)=2\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391143 1072 #uuid "ecd7ba84-c62d-5665-b104-2afa83226b1f" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391143 1074 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2} \\\\  & =({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2} \\\\ {{{y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-y-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-y-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.$ Therefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-2-(2)^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-2-4 \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391144 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391145 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391144 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391146 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391144 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391147 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391144 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391148 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391144 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391149 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391144 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391144 1077 "selection" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391144 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391147 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391144 1080 #uuid "6856b1da-9b23-517a-a9e0-8ccdcf647ba0" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391145 1081 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+6" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391145 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391145 1084 #uuid "90c43c9d-da3b-5cc5-aff8-5e064531ce24" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391146 1081 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391146 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391146 1084 #uuid "9f671a2c-e2b8-5d20-b384-708b60c2aa83" 13194139533463 17592186045585 true] [17592186391147 1081 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-6" 13